From 8cdfcde6d4bbc55b172c28edd6db7e68ff6cd904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:15:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] gugu: _session/steering extension method (mid-turn
 message injection)

Adds an ACP extension method with the same name and contract as
@agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp's and pi-acp's, so a client can add a
message to the RUNNING turn instead of preempting it: injected (turn running)
/ promptRequired + noRunningTurn (idle, client opted in via
_meta.steering.idleBehavior) / startedNewTurn (idle). The running case uses
the backend's own steer path, `v4/command sendText` with
`requestedDelivery: "guide"`: app-server 0.16.9 folds the text into the
running turn at its next tool boundary - one turn, no cancellation.
initialize() advertises `_meta.steering.supported = true`.

Why: Gugu delivers group messages that arrive mid-turn this way. Without it a
second session/prompt preempts the in-flight prompt, which then reports
`cancelled` although its work went on (measured live: first prompt
stopReason=cancelled at +8 s, final reply carried both instructions).
With the patch: first prompt end_turn, steering answered injected at +8 s,
reply "A-DONE BANANA" (ZCode 3.15.3, CLI 0.16.9).

Upstream: not filed - owner 10-17: kept and maintained here only (see
bridges/zcode-acp/PATCHES.md for the upstream code it touches).

Drop when: upstream ships `_session/steering` (or an equivalent) in the tag
this is built on.
